# NOTICES

Third-party attribution notices for Brilliancy.

## The convention (spec §2.3)

**Any dependency carrying an attribution requirement is added to this file in the
same commit that adds the dependency. Never later.**

A dependency added without its NOTICES entry is an incomplete commit, and every
commit on a feature branch has to stand on its own (§0.2) — so the entry cannot
be deferred to a follow-up.

Scope:

- Listed here: anything with an attribution requirement that is **distributed to
  users** — shipped in the browser bundle, embedded as a static asset, vendored
  into the repository, or baked into a server image. This includes, at minimum,
  the MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, ISC, CC-BY, CC-BY-SA and
  GPL/LGPL/AGPL families.
- Also listed: vendored public-domain data (CC0, Unlicense). There is no legal
  requirement, but provenance of vendored data is worth recording — see §2.5.
- Not listed: development-only tooling that is never distributed (the compiler,
  the test runner, the linter, the build orchestrator).

Each entry records the package or asset, its SPDX licence identifier, and the
source URL. Transitive dependencies that ship to users are listed too — the
obligation follows the bytes, not the `package.json`.

## Brilliancy itself

Brilliancy is licensed **AGPL-3.0-or-later**. The full text is in `LICENSE`.

Copyright (C) 2026 Brilliancy contributors.

Brilliancy is offered to users over a network, so AGPL §13 applies: any operator
of a modified version must offer that version's users its corresponding source.
See `README.md`.

## Runtime dependencies distributed to users

None. Nothing in this repository is shipped to a user yet.

## Not yet dependencies

Deliberately empty. Stockfish (GPL-3.0-or-later), `@lichess-org/chessground`
(GPL-3.0-or-later), `chess.js`, the `lichess-org/chess-openings` ECO data (CC0)
and the Cburnett piece set (CC-BY-SA 3.0) are all named in §0.2 and §2.5 as
future dependencies, and each gets its entry above in the commit that adds it —
not before, and not in a follow-up.
